<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador posts $77 mln trade surplus in February.</title>
<headline>Ecuador posts $77 mln trade surplus in February.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador posted a $77 million trade surplus in February, up from the $72 million surplus during the same month last year, the Central Bank said Wednesday.</p>
<p>Exports reached $372 million, up from $347 million in February 1996. Imports grew to $295 million from $275 million.</p>
<p>In the first two months of 1997, there was a $62 million surplus versus an $87 million surplus in the same 1996 period.</p>
<p>((--Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258429, e-mail: reuters1@reutersecu.com.ec))</p>
